Source: stoat-desktop
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), unzip, desktop-file-utils
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/stoatchat/for-desktop

Package: stoat-desktop
Architecture: amd64
# Runtime set: the payload's ELF DT_NEEDED union (readelf over every
# shipped ELF; bundled ffmpeg excluded). libsecret covers Electron
# safeStorage (dlopen); libudev1 is the true provider of libudev.so.1.
# t64 names target Debian Testing.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, hicolor-icon-theme, libasound2t64, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libatspi2.0-0, libcairo2, libcups2t64, libdbus-1-3, libexpat1, libgbm1, libglib2.0-0t64, libgtk-3-0t64, libnspr4, libnss3, libpango-1.0-0, libpipewire-0.3-0, libsecret-1-0, libudev1, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxkbcommon0, libxrandr2, xdg-utils
Description: Open source, user-first chat platform desktop client
 Stoat is an open source, user-first chat platform. Send messages, share
 images, mention users, and join voice channels.
